mission "The Company Beneath the Sand"
    name "The Company Beneath the Sand"
    description "Uncover the modern syndicate financing the search and free its imprisoned mapmaker."
    source "Redoubt"
    destination "Sugarhook"
    reward 1915
    speaker offer "Mapmaker Jules Ardent"
    speaker visit "Mapmaker Jules Ardent"
    speaker complete "Mapmaker Jules Ardent"
    to offer
        has "The Captain's Other Journal: done"
    on offer
        conversation
            `The mapmaker's name has been struck from the syndicate's papers. Jules Ardent is being held at Sugarhook, while the men financing the search keep their own names out of the ledgers.`
            `Ardent's last message reached the council through a dockworker. "They hired me to copy the old charts, then locked me away when I started asking why the same islands were missing from every version. I can tell you who paid for the work, but first I need to get out."`
            choice
                `"I will hear the whole story, then take the work."`
                    accept
                `"What have the records left out?"`
                    goto details
                `"There are limits to what I will take on. This is one."`
                    close
            label details
                `The note is brief, but the warning is plain. "The syndicate is buying the search quietly. Free me and we can follow the payments back to the people who want the drowned settlement found—and owned."`
                choice
                    `"You can rely on me. I will start at once."`
                        accept
                    `"No. Do not wait for me."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Company Beneath the Sand. Uncover the modern syndicate financing the search and free its imprisoned mapmaker."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Sugarhook, Jules is free and has recovered the account book. The entries identify the syndicate that financed the search. "They were not paying for scholarship," Ardent says. "They wanted the map before anyone else could see it."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Ardent holds the account book against his chest. "I will testify about the money and the charts. The men who paid for this thought a mapmaker could be bought and buried. They were wrong about both."`
        log "Completed The Company Beneath the Sand. Received 1915 gold. Uncover the modern syndicate financing the search and free its imprisoned mapmaker."
